WEBVTT

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.450
You're beautiful...

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.480
I'll take you to the flower garden.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:31.010
Remo.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:33.370
Grandma!

00:02:05.110 --> 00:02:06.100
Dual!

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:20.450
I did it! I won first prize! I can't believe it!

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:24.920
Well done.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:29.790
I can finally go to London in the spring!
Maybe I can even study there!

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:31.750
Your dream might come true.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:38.380
Yeah! I've always dreamed of traveling
the world and playing piano for everyone!

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:42.170
You've always been there for me.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:44.760
Thank you so much.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:48.770
I couldn't have made it this far without you.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:51.140
Sumire...

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:54.440
I'm sorry.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.190
What?

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:58.230
This backup data

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.110
is infected with a virus.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.120
It can't be restored.

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:09.790
I'm not the Dual that you know.

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:14.190
This is a backup copy of 21st-century Japan.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:17.050
A virtual world being stored
within the Box of Wisdom.

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:20.050
Is something wrong?

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:23.680
We're out of time.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:31.680
What?!

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:36.270
This world has been completely infected by a virus.

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:41.990
And so have you, Sumire.

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:48.540
No way! What's going on?!

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:51.540
Deleting data!

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:10.320
What is this?

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:14.900
Is this some sort of dream?

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:17.740
Am I dreaming?

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:19.320
It isn't.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:23.040
The world you were living in,
however, was a dream.

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:24.570
A dream...

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:29.300
It was all a dream. You and I are both just data.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:35.050
What are you saying? You're Dual.
We've always been together!

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:36.860
For you, it may seem that way.

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:41.860
However, I reconstructed
this world only a short while ago.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:46.720
You and your memories are nothing
but recently re-assembled data.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.300
I don't get what you're saying!

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.850
Infected data...

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:54.600
must be deleted.

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:43.360
What are you playing at?

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:46.660
What do you mean?

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:47.950
What do I mean?

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:49.720
Don't play dumb with me!

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:51.400
Get yourself together!

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:54.050
That world was supposed to be mine!

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:55.130
I guess.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:56.090
You guess?

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:59.380
There you go again! Stick to the rules!

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:01.240
I've been waiting for ages.

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:02.370
Didn't you see?

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:03.710
See what?!

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:06.670
I was meant to delete that world.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:08.940
What?

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:12.840
Sumire believed I was her childhood friend.

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:14.850
So it had to be me.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:18.190
What, you felt some kind of
responsibility toward her or something?

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:26.890
I mean, sure, you were supposed
to be her friend in that world,

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:31.620
but ultimately, she was just a scrap of
human data in a virtual world program.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:34.290
A world that was only just
recently reconstructed, too.

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:40.060
Why do you bother sulking over every deletion?

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:43.370
Just hurry up and delete that data, too.

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:48.980
It's been happening a lot since the upgrade...

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:54.380
Us getting integrated into reconstructed worlds

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:55.890
as a friend or a family member.

00:06:56.570 --> 00:06:58.900
It never used to happen before.

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:02.450
Humans do the most annoying things.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:06.530
She said her dream was to become a pianist.

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:08.110
Her dream, huh?

00:07:09.170 --> 00:07:12.200
Not that I understand.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:16.990
You've been acting strange lately.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:20.330
You're getting attached to data
that's meant to be deleted.

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:22.310
We're just programs.

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:25.370
All we need to do is get rid of viruses
in accordance with our algorithms.

00:07:26.030 --> 00:07:28.050
Man, this is getting on my nerves!

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:33.710
This is happening because
we're both anti-virus software.

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:36.900
Why did they install both of us?

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:42.230
Maybe they're trying to see which one is superior?

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:45.480
In that case, I'd win. Hands down.

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:46.440
My, aren't you talkative?

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:49.400
Maybe you've been infected.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.490
I'd rather say that <i>you</i>
have a bug in <i>your</i> system!

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:00.200
Dorothy!

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:01.440
Shut it!

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:01.870
Huh?

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:03.450
Who's that?

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:09.550
Hey! Don't run off on your own again!

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:12.840
Deleting data.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.470
Bring it on!

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:29.330
There are so many viruses lately!

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:30.530
You hear that, you creeps?

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:34.280
I miss the days when we were
just fixing bugs in the system.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:48.260
Almost done.

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:58.450
Get out of my way!

00:08:58.450 --> 00:08:59.470
You get out!

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:03.140
Compress.

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:04.190
Shut up!

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:14.870
Delete.

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:22.160
That was a tough one.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:26.230
I could have handled it myself though.

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:28.490
I feel like there have been more viruses lately.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:32.380
You're right. It's pretty weird.

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:33.990
Where are they all coming from?

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:41.060
Hey, she doesn't seem to be infected.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:45.140
No virus detected.

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:48.840
Could be a Trojan.

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:51.730
We should delete her, just in case.

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:56.030
We're not authorized to delete this program.

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:57.110
Wait a second.

00:09:57.110 --> 00:09:59.150
Don't tell me you're taking her with you?

00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:02.720
Fixing bugs is part of our job, too.

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:04.830
I know, but come on!

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:11.730
Hey!

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:25.970
Don't you think you're being mean, Dual?

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:26.920
How so?

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:30.390
I can't enter without your permission.

00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:34.070
Go back to your own zone. I'll stay with her.

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:35.620
Are you crazy?

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:39.820
If she's some new breed of virus,
my zone might get infected too!

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:46.660
What a pain!

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:51.000
If you weren't around,
I'd have this place all to myself...

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:54.100
Wh-What?!

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:03.120
Wh-What's happening?!

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:17.230
She fell asleep?

00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:25.870
Who are you?

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:29.980
I'm Dual.

00:11:30.550 --> 00:11:33.420
You were attacked by a virus, weren't you?

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:36.140
What are you?

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:40.100
Are you an anti-virus program like us?

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:42.720
You're a virus, right? Just admit it.

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:48.810
We told you who we are!
The least you can do is tell us your name!

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:50.640
Remo...

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:54.230
Remo? Is that your name?

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:57.760
What kind of program are you?

00:11:58.370 --> 00:11:59.360
Flower...

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:01.030
Flower?

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:03.970
I have to return to the flower garden...

00:12:03.970 --> 00:12:07.350
Where? Is that some place in the backup data?

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:08.930
I...

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:11.370
I...

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:14.460
Why were you installed in the Box of Wisdom?

00:12:15.320 --> 00:12:17.280
What are you programmed to do?

00:12:26.730 --> 00:12:28.760
This is really weird.

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:31.710
She's an anomaly. She's suspicious.

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:35.730
She's also dangerous.
It'd be a good idea to delete her.

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:39.340
We can't delete data that isn't infected.

00:12:39.340 --> 00:12:42.580
We can quarantine her or something, though.

00:12:42.580 --> 00:12:44.940
Programs can't act on their own free will.

00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:48.250
If we just did whatever we wanted,
we'd be no different from viruses.

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:55.180
I think she's just unstable right now.
She might recover on her own in due time.

00:12:55.180 --> 00:12:56.750
I'm telling you, Dual.

00:12:57.390 --> 00:13:00.090
If that girl is a virus,
we'll have to delete her right away,

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:01.590
or else we'll be in danger, too.

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:03.010
I know.

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:14.540
Level One?

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:17.380
Right. This is Level One.

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:20.850
Besides Dorothy and me,
you're the first to set foot in here.

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:24.280
The Box of Wisdom is divided into three levels.

00:13:24.980 --> 00:13:27.210
We found you in Level Two.

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:30.260
That's where all the backup data is pooled.

00:13:30.260 --> 00:13:32.120
Backup data?

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:37.040
Restorable data for various time periods and places.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:41.360
Dorothy and I are in charge of
monitoring the Box of Wisdom.

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:44.170
If we find any bugs or defects, we fix them.

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:47.520
If a virus appears, we compress and delete it.

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:51.340
We access the archived data and scan it for viruses.

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:05.530
This is all backup data.

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:09.940
Virtual reproductions of various eras and lands.

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:12.490
What's this?

00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:14.130
Don't be scared.

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:16.960
It's the remains of a virus we dealt with.

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:19.600
We compress it

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:22.600
and then delete it.

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:28.390
So if I were a virus, like Dorothy said...

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:32.020
You aren't a virus.

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:37.870
Do you want to see a virus scan?

00:14:39.180 --> 00:14:40.960
You may remember something.

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:00.580
Whoa!

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:03.330
She's so cute! Is she a celebrity?

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:06.850
This is Level Three.

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:11.280
This world, along with everyone living in it,

00:15:11.280 --> 00:15:13.080
only just came into existence.

00:15:20.010 --> 00:15:21.770
Do you recognize anything here?

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:27.850
Not really. I wonder why I got so excited.

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:29.890
Did you remember something?

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:31.780
No.

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:35.510
I'm sorry. I wasted your time...

00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:37.510
That's okay.

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:40.780
I just felt like eating something.

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:43.790
This looks so yummy!

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:46.000
Yummy?

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:59.650
I guess a human would
find things delicious or cold.

00:16:00.320 --> 00:16:01.480
You don't?

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:05.180
Delicious, beautiful, fun, interesting.

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:10.330
I understand the concepts,
but I can't experience them.

00:16:10.330 --> 00:16:13.710
Anti-virus programs have
no use for such functions.

00:16:13.710 --> 00:16:16.500
What about feeling joy or sadness?

00:16:19.990 --> 00:16:21.010
I don't know.

00:16:21.670 --> 00:16:24.630
I think I've felt something close...

00:16:25.410 --> 00:16:27.410
I guess humans call them "emotions",

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:31.090
but I'm not sure if what I felt was that.

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:34.550
Perhaps human data has emotions,

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:38.330
as well as memories and dreams.

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:39.690
Dreams?

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:43.990
But those are only programmed in.

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:46.240
You're amazing, Remo.

00:16:46.890 --> 00:16:48.370
Can you taste things?

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:52.690
I get the feeling it's probably delicious.

00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:56.380
Maybe you're human data.

00:16:56.380 --> 00:16:57.490
I don't know.

00:16:57.490 --> 00:17:00.750
But if you tell yourself something is delicious,
doesn't that make it delicious?

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:04.870
It does seem delicious if I tell myself it is...

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:07.500
Delicious, huh?

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:10.700
You guys know what that feels like?

00:17:10.700 --> 00:17:12.260
You went and reconstructed another one!

00:17:12.620 --> 00:17:14.940
I told you it was my turn!

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:16.930
I wanted to show Remo.

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:19.250
You always do as you please.

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:21.890
This is fun.

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:25.070
So, did you figure out where the flower garden is?

00:17:25.070 --> 00:17:25.970
No.

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:28.290
I knew it.

00:17:32.060 --> 00:17:34.050
Hurry up and remember!

00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:45.330
These humans don't know that their existence

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:47.170
is like a dream.

00:17:47.930 --> 00:17:50.380
Who made the Box of Wisdom?

00:17:51.140 --> 00:17:53.780
Why back up data of different times and places?

00:17:53.780 --> 00:17:56.510
And even the humans who live there?

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:58.750
Who would do that, and for what purpose?

00:17:59.200 --> 00:18:02.680
No idea. We just do the job
we were programmed to do.

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:07.500
I'm glad this place wasn't infected.

00:18:08.580 --> 00:18:10.650
What if it was?

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:15.110
I'd have to compress the whole world and delete it.

00:18:18.350 --> 00:18:22.240
So, the real world exists outside this Box, right?

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:23.500
"The real world"?

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:26.110
The reality where humans live.

00:18:27.610 --> 00:18:28.750
I guess.

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:30.270
We can't see it, though.

00:18:30.980 --> 00:18:32.850
Do you want to talk to them?

00:18:32.850 --> 00:18:35.250
To the humans who created us?

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:36.550
To humans?

00:18:39.810 --> 00:18:41.590
I'd never even thought about it.

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:44.500
You have such an imagination.

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:47.120
Really?

00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:50.980
Am I a weird program?

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:04.620
Remo.

00:19:13.890 --> 00:19:15.500
I feel like cleaning!

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:47.830
Morning!

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:49.330
Pleasant dreams?

00:19:49.780 --> 00:19:50.900
We don't dream.

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:55.400
For us, sleep means shutting down to upgrade.

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:56.730
I see.

00:19:56.730 --> 00:20:02.140
When one of us upgrades,
the other one upgrades automatically.

00:20:02.140 --> 00:20:05.280
Humans provide us with upgrades.

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:06.950
Humans do?

00:20:07.910 --> 00:20:08.960
What's wrong?

00:20:08.960 --> 00:20:12.430
N-Nothing. I just...

00:20:12.430 --> 00:20:14.060
What are you doing?

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:16.020
Cooking!

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:19.180
I wanted to make something for you.

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:23.450
Dig in!

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:27.990
Why are we doing this?

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:29.750
Don't ask me.

00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:33.920
I just had an urge to cook.

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:35.890
Where did you get the ingredients?

00:20:35.890 --> 00:20:38.000
From the backup data.

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:41.080
What? Don't you start doing as you please too!

00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:44.680
Once I got started, it was so much fun!

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:47.210
She didn't bring back any viruses, did she?

00:20:49.410 --> 00:20:50.800
Nope, I guess not.

00:20:50.800 --> 00:20:52.190
So? How is it?

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:57.260
We can't tell if it tastes good or not.

00:20:57.260 --> 00:20:59.230
I guess that's true...

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:01.880
But if I tell myself it's delicious, it seems like it is.

00:21:01.880 --> 00:21:02.770
Really?

00:21:02.770 --> 00:21:03.710
Yeah.

00:21:03.710 --> 00:21:06.660
Yay! Dorothy, you try it too!

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:09.640
I have no interest in human culture.

00:21:09.640 --> 00:21:10.930
Come on!

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:13.200
I see you don't trust your own virus scan.

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:15.760
What? Are you kidding?

00:21:21.060 --> 00:21:24.340
Well, I guess I could find this
delicious if I tell myself it is.

00:21:24.340 --> 00:21:26.400
That's great!

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:28.200
Is that really something to be happy about?

00:21:29.640 --> 00:21:32.740
Hold it! I can wipe my own mouth!

00:21:36.300 --> 00:21:37.060
You're good.

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:38.770
You brought these, too?

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:39.980
Yeah.

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:42.730
I like the data from this place.

00:21:42.730 --> 00:21:45.940
Look! I can juggle three of them!

00:21:47.290 --> 00:21:49.220
Even I can do that much.

00:22:02.640 --> 00:22:03.930
What's that tune?

00:22:04.770 --> 00:22:06.510
Schubert's Lullaby.

00:22:08.550 --> 00:22:10.540
You have some strange talents.

00:22:12.010 --> 00:22:13.920
They're strange?

00:22:14.440 --> 00:22:18.980
At the very least,
you're not anti-virus software like us.

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:20.690
When I'm with you,

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:24.960
I almost understand how delicious
food tastes or how beautiful music sounds.

00:22:26.370 --> 00:22:30.570
That's probably because I
find them delicious and beautiful,

00:22:30.570 --> 00:22:33.310
and those feelings reach both of you.

00:22:33.310 --> 00:22:34.280
Both of us?

00:22:34.280 --> 00:22:35.970
Is that how it works?

00:22:35.970 --> 00:22:38.660
Yeah. It means our hearts are in sync.

00:22:42.850 --> 00:22:45.230
Is there a song you want to hear?

00:22:45.740 --> 00:22:49.470
I told you. We don't understand music.

00:22:49.470 --> 00:22:51.280
Do you know this one?

00:23:02.330 --> 00:23:03.320
How can you play it?

00:23:03.780 --> 00:23:04.790
I don't know.

00:23:07.550 --> 00:23:12.940
My dream is to become
a pianist and travel the world.

00:23:12.940 --> 00:23:18.280
Music can transcend time and borders
to bring people together, right?

00:23:18.280 --> 00:23:22.420
I want to do that with my music one day.

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:25.300
Piano can make miracles happen.

00:23:27.420 --> 00:23:29.380
That's all I remember.

00:23:30.270 --> 00:23:32.190
Looks like my memory's a little fuzzy.

00:23:33.710 --> 00:23:35.470
What's wrong, Dual?

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:37.100
Are you crying?

00:23:38.150 --> 00:23:42.400
We never cry, because we don't need to.

00:23:42.400 --> 00:23:45.580
Don't worry. It's not your fault.

00:23:46.730 --> 00:23:48.860
Sorry. I'm fine.

00:23:49.450 --> 00:23:51.030
Can you play it again?

00:23:51.450 --> 00:23:54.590
But I don't know the rest.

00:23:55.490 --> 00:23:56.630
That's fine.

00:23:56.630 --> 00:23:57.660
If you say so.

00:24:12.790 --> 00:24:17.350
I still think you're a fragment
of human data from somewhere.

00:24:17.350 --> 00:24:19.270
Human data?

00:24:19.270 --> 00:24:24.900
Yeah. You must've come out of
one of the backups stored here.

00:24:27.390 --> 00:24:31.360
How else would you know
so much about human culture?

00:24:31.870 --> 00:24:35.370
Yeah. You do have a point.

00:24:35.370 --> 00:24:37.400
Right?

00:24:40.520 --> 00:24:44.940
You probably came from some
flower garden. I'm sure of it.

00:24:46.240 --> 00:24:48.000
Man, I'm so brilliant!

00:24:50.860 --> 00:24:51.830
What's so funny?

00:24:52.360 --> 00:24:53.400
Nothing.

00:24:53.400 --> 00:24:57.530
It just hit me that you're worried about me, too.

00:24:57.530 --> 00:24:59.390
I'm not worried at all!

00:24:59.390 --> 00:25:03.060
I just can't rest easy unless I know who you are.

00:25:03.060 --> 00:25:04.070
That's all.

00:25:05.300 --> 00:25:09.610
It's gonna be a pain to check
every single backup here.

00:25:10.130 --> 00:25:12.230
We can scan for viruses at the same time.

00:25:12.230 --> 00:25:13.770
I guess...

00:25:14.860 --> 00:25:18.120
We don't want her getting lost again, though...

00:25:19.380 --> 00:25:21.270
You're still holding on to that?

00:25:21.910 --> 00:25:25.500
If we use this as a tag,
we can find Remo wherever she is.

00:25:30.250 --> 00:25:32.550
I think it'd look better on you, Dual.

00:25:33.890 --> 00:25:37.080
It's a memento from a girl named Sumire.

00:25:37.080 --> 00:25:38.050
Sumire?

00:25:39.040 --> 00:25:42.080
Human data that Dual was friends with.

00:25:42.630 --> 00:25:45.140
But she was infected, so we had to delete her.

00:25:55.780 --> 00:25:58.740
Thanks. I'll take good care of it.

00:26:03.040 --> 00:26:04.250
What?

00:26:04.250 --> 00:26:05.940
We're like three sisters.

00:26:06.610 --> 00:26:09.300
You're one strange program.

00:26:09.920 --> 00:26:12.170
Let's go!

00:26:33.360 --> 00:26:44.790
When time was flowing so softly and quietly

00:26:47.290 --> 00:26:59.050
I thought that all we needed to do was protect this world

00:26:59.550 --> 00:27:00.600
But then...

00:27:00.600 --> 00:27:07.430
My heart became one with yours

00:27:07.430 --> 00:27:17.160
It was full of feelings I wanted to share with you

00:27:17.160 --> 00:27:25.000
I have so many great memories of our own world

00:27:25.000 --> 00:27:31.880
A world so perfect and beautiful

00:27:31.880 --> 00:27:37.590
So if you feel at least a little bit happy

00:27:37.590 --> 00:27:43.170
Then I would be really happy too

00:27:43.760 --> 00:27:48.190
Let us talk some more

00:27:48.810 --> 00:27:57.450
So you can feel the same way I do

00:29:38.090 --> 00:29:42.680
My frozen heart has begun to awaken

00:29:42.680 --> 00:29:47.920
I want to feel more, learn more, and experience more

00:29:49.220 --> 00:29:57.660
Being alone was such a natural thing to me

00:29:59.530 --> 00:30:07.780
But now that I know how it feels to have friends

00:30:07.780 --> 00:30:15.740
I'm not as I was programmed to be

00:30:16.080 --> 00:30:21.290
I'm seeing the world in different colors

00:30:21.420 --> 00:30:26.140
I want you to tell me about all the things I don't yet know

00:30:26.140 --> 00:30:32.140
With the magic of your words I would learn all about things like

00:30:32.140 --> 00:30:36.230
Happiness, sadness, loneliness, and joy!

00:30:36.230 --> 00:30:42.280
And somehow, in some way, it would make me feel alive

00:30:42.280 --> 00:30:46.570
Ah, I want these feelings to engulf me!

00:30:46.570 --> 00:30:50.160
I want to feel them all

00:30:50.160 --> 00:30:52.500
Because it seems like so much fun!

00:30:52.500 --> 00:30:59.210
Smiling with everyone will surely bring me happiness

00:31:09.720 --> 00:31:13.890
It really does make me so happy...

00:31:19.670 --> 00:31:23.310
Happy birthday, Dorothy!

00:31:24.020 --> 00:31:26.670
Here's my present to you...

00:31:26.670 --> 00:31:27.490
A hat!

00:31:27.490 --> 00:31:29.630
I thought it would look good on you.

00:31:31.150 --> 00:31:32.080
It's beautiful!

00:31:32.080 --> 00:31:33.450
I got you some candy.

00:31:33.820 --> 00:31:36.030
You love sweets, right?

00:31:37.220 --> 00:31:38.710
I love them!

00:31:38.710 --> 00:31:40.370
And this is from Mommy.

00:31:40.370 --> 00:31:43.490
I think you'd look nice in a dress like this now.

00:31:43.490 --> 00:31:44.960
Mom made it herself.

00:31:44.960 --> 00:31:46.840
She'd been working on it for ages.

00:31:46.840 --> 00:31:49.360
We helped a little, too.

00:31:49.360 --> 00:31:50.440
Thank you!

00:31:51.210 --> 00:31:53.300
And this is from Daddy.

00:31:53.300 --> 00:31:54.300
Oh, my!

00:31:59.430 --> 00:32:00.420
A puppy!

00:32:00.420 --> 00:32:01.560
How cute!

00:32:01.560 --> 00:32:04.900
You've wanted one for a long time.
Take good care of him.

00:32:04.900 --> 00:32:06.860
Thank you.

00:32:06.860 --> 00:32:09.050
Okay, Dorothy.

00:32:09.050 --> 00:32:12.440
They say that if you make a wish as you
blow out the candles, it'll come true.

00:32:12.440 --> 00:32:14.140
What's your dream, Dorothy?

00:32:15.840 --> 00:32:17.200
Well...

00:32:17.200 --> 00:32:21.210
I want us to be happy together forever!

00:32:26.860 --> 00:32:27.830
Dorothy...

00:32:28.400 --> 00:32:31.990
That world was infected by a virus.

00:32:31.990 --> 00:32:34.090
I had to delete it.

00:32:34.490 --> 00:32:37.040
They were just programmed data,

00:32:37.040 --> 00:32:40.180
but they truly believed that
I was part of their family.

00:32:56.640 --> 00:32:57.680
Dorothy...

00:32:58.260 --> 00:32:59.420
I'm fine.

00:33:00.510 --> 00:33:01.740
That cake...

00:33:03.090 --> 00:33:05.310
If I'd eaten the one my mom made...

00:33:06.610 --> 00:33:08.540
I'm sure it would have been delicious.

00:33:12.120 --> 00:33:16.090
I'm getting just as weird as you guys.

00:33:17.400 --> 00:33:19.300
I don't get it.

00:33:19.880 --> 00:33:22.060
Why does backup data exist?

00:33:22.060 --> 00:33:26.020
Only the humans who created
the Box of Wisdom would know.

00:33:26.470 --> 00:33:30.800
Where do viruses come from?
Why did they suddenly increase in number?

00:33:30.800 --> 00:33:33.190
Does infected data really have to be deleted?

00:33:33.190 --> 00:33:35.530
Is there no other way...?

00:33:35.910 --> 00:33:39.740
Our role is to do what we've
been programmed to do.

00:33:40.640 --> 00:33:44.250
There's too much I don't
understand about this world.

00:33:44.830 --> 00:33:49.210
Why am I even here?

00:33:50.960 --> 00:33:54.170
I still love this world, though.

00:33:54.520 --> 00:33:56.060
That's why I've protected it for all this time,

00:33:56.980 --> 00:33:58.250
and I'll keep on doing so.

00:34:04.960 --> 00:34:08.820
Keep it down. You woke me up.

00:34:08.820 --> 00:34:12.090
For some reason, housework really calms me down.

00:34:12.090 --> 00:34:15.400
You sure have it nice. You don't have to upgrade.

00:34:16.010 --> 00:34:18.320
It doesn't matter if you sleep or not.

00:34:18.710 --> 00:34:22.830
Maybe you're just a support tool for us.

00:34:22.830 --> 00:34:26.150
Maybe the flower garden isn't even real.

00:34:26.840 --> 00:34:28.730
The flower garden...

00:34:28.730 --> 00:34:32.250
I feel like it's something important...

00:34:36.290 --> 00:34:38.180
A support tool, huh?

00:34:38.180 --> 00:34:40.480
I hope that's true.

00:34:40.480 --> 00:34:41.740
Why?

00:34:41.740 --> 00:34:44.390
That means we can be together forever.

00:34:47.730 --> 00:34:49.850
A moderate-level virus alert.

00:34:50.650 --> 00:34:53.900
Where are they all coming from?

00:34:53.900 --> 00:34:55.050
Stay here, Remo.

00:34:55.050 --> 00:34:57.090
Why? I want to come.

00:34:56.500 --> 00:34:59.820
Don't bother. You'd just get in the way.

00:34:58.480 --> 00:34:59.820
That's mean!

00:35:16.260 --> 00:35:17.050
A new variant?

00:35:18.510 --> 00:35:20.050
I've never seen this type before.

00:35:26.490 --> 00:35:28.480
Still a piece of cake, though!

00:35:31.900 --> 00:35:33.020
Compress!

00:35:41.380 --> 00:35:42.340
And delete.

00:35:43.920 --> 00:35:47.050
I wonder what happens to the viruses we delete...

00:35:48.180 --> 00:35:51.080
Deleting them means that they just disappear.

00:35:51.080 --> 00:35:52.710
Why do you care?

00:35:53.100 --> 00:35:55.170
I remembered what Remo once said.

00:35:58.890 --> 00:36:01.570
I think you're going crazy.

00:36:02.580 --> 00:36:03.640
Another one?

00:36:09.830 --> 00:36:10.560
It's huge!

00:36:15.340 --> 00:36:16.570
It's all yours!

00:36:22.290 --> 00:36:23.950
What are you doing?!

00:36:25.160 --> 00:36:26.320
Give it back...

00:36:27.440 --> 00:36:28.780
Sumire!

00:36:28.780 --> 00:36:31.620
Please give it back...

00:36:33.690 --> 00:36:37.000
Give me back my dream.

00:36:37.000 --> 00:36:37.860
Your dream?

00:36:39.440 --> 00:36:41.820
Sumire's dream?

00:36:48.310 --> 00:36:50.680
What are you spacing out for?!

00:36:55.310 --> 00:36:56.810
You and your stupid functions...

00:36:58.270 --> 00:36:59.230
Dual!

00:37:02.060 --> 00:37:03.070
Dorothy...

00:37:03.690 --> 00:37:06.460
If I get infected, eliminate me...

00:37:07.560 --> 00:37:10.290
Take care of Remo.

00:37:10.290 --> 00:37:11.870
Stop talking nonsense!

00:37:13.940 --> 00:37:15.150
I'm coming to save you!

00:37:15.680 --> 00:37:18.040
Dorothy! Dual!

00:37:19.000 --> 00:37:21.980
You idiot! Why did you follow us?

00:37:21.980 --> 00:37:22.760
I just...

00:37:25.500 --> 00:37:26.220
What?

00:37:30.640 --> 00:37:31.660
Remo!

00:37:49.920 --> 00:37:52.330
Remo! Remo!

00:38:08.220 --> 00:38:09.090
Where's Remo?

00:38:14.750 --> 00:38:15.680
Over there!

00:38:20.920 --> 00:38:22.330
She's not infected.

00:38:23.120 --> 00:38:24.800
Let me check you, too.

00:38:26.240 --> 00:38:27.450
You're clean.

00:38:27.660 --> 00:38:28.990
What does this mean?

00:38:29.640 --> 00:38:32.980
I thought the virus infiltrated both of you...

00:38:32.980 --> 00:38:35.440
What happened to the virus?

00:38:36.040 --> 00:38:37.080
I don't know.

00:38:38.720 --> 00:38:40.540
There was this bright light...

00:38:40.540 --> 00:38:42.090
And now there's no sign of it.

00:38:54.600 --> 00:38:56.980
Maybe she's infected after all.

00:38:57.350 --> 00:38:58.400
I don't detect anything.

00:38:59.550 --> 00:39:01.440
Maybe her memory's coming back.

00:39:02.900 --> 00:39:04.860
Did you say "Sumire" earlier?

00:39:05.500 --> 00:39:08.900
I saw her inside the virus.

00:39:08.900 --> 00:39:11.160
But wasn't she deleted?

00:39:13.770 --> 00:39:15.980
Deleted viruses are destroyed.

00:39:16.630 --> 00:39:18.960
That's what we always thought.

00:39:18.960 --> 00:39:23.040
Right. They cease to exist in the Box of Wisdom.

00:39:23.040 --> 00:39:24.350
That's the end of it.

00:39:25.260 --> 00:39:27.970
But what if it's not?

00:39:27.970 --> 00:39:33.100
I'm starting to wonder about things
I've never even considered before.

00:39:36.140 --> 00:39:38.980
When the virus engulfed me...

00:39:38.980 --> 00:39:39.770
What about it?

00:39:40.410 --> 00:39:42.230
You tried to help me.

00:39:43.160 --> 00:39:44.050
Thank you.

00:39:45.690 --> 00:39:46.710
Whatever.

00:39:51.610 --> 00:39:55.490
Connecting to the host. Initializing remote link.

00:39:55.800 --> 00:39:56.950
Remo!

00:39:57.290 --> 00:40:01.170
Measuring virtual coordinates
of the Box of Wisdom.

00:40:02.150 --> 00:40:05.920
Separating protocol. Initiating search.

00:40:05.920 --> 00:40:07.170
Remo!

00:40:07.960 --> 00:40:09.810
Remo, who are you?

00:40:10.390 --> 00:40:12.930
Why were you installed in the Box of Wisdom?

00:40:14.260 --> 00:40:18.730
To search and collect data.

00:40:18.730 --> 00:40:20.580
Data? What data?

00:40:21.200 --> 00:40:23.960
Data for an experiment.

00:40:24.730 --> 00:40:28.790
What experiment?
What do humans want from you?

00:40:29.470 --> 00:40:32.210
Not humans...

00:40:33.480 --> 00:40:36.610
Then who programmed you?

00:40:37.210 --> 00:40:40.060
Humans are probably...

00:40:40.060 --> 00:40:42.120
all... de...

00:40:44.180 --> 00:40:45.880
Did you understand that?

00:40:48.490 --> 00:40:49.310
Hey.

00:40:50.160 --> 00:40:55.090
Dorothy, how much time
has passed since our installation?

00:40:55.090 --> 00:40:58.890
Dunno. I've never checked...

00:40:58.890 --> 00:41:01.720
Uh, five years?

00:41:02.780 --> 00:41:07.900
Maybe time inside the box flows at
a different rate than it does outside.

00:41:08.730 --> 00:41:13.360
Like how time in backup data flows at
a different rate than here in Level One.

00:41:15.070 --> 00:41:19.580
Perhaps far more time has
passed in the outside world.

00:41:20.320 --> 00:41:22.100
Fifty or maybe even a hundred years...

00:41:22.650 --> 00:41:24.320
Perhaps even more.

00:41:24.320 --> 00:41:26.670
What are you thinking?

00:41:27.640 --> 00:41:29.420
Remo! Remo!

00:41:34.680 --> 00:41:37.830
She's not going to stay like this, is she?

00:41:39.580 --> 00:41:41.460
Is there anything you need?

00:41:44.420 --> 00:41:46.150
Piano...

00:41:46.150 --> 00:41:47.630
Did she just say piano?

00:41:48.460 --> 00:41:49.890
That tune...

00:41:50.610 --> 00:41:52.890
Does she want to hear that lullaby?

00:41:52.890 --> 00:41:53.940
Could it be?

00:41:54.350 --> 00:41:55.860
What are you doing?

00:41:55.860 --> 00:41:59.780
Remo appeared when I deleted Sumire's world.

00:41:59.780 --> 00:42:03.250
That song may trigger something in her memory.

00:42:03.580 --> 00:42:05.540
You can play the piano?

00:42:06.480 --> 00:42:08.000
Enough to make a sound.

00:42:08.600 --> 00:42:10.630
I watched Remo play.

00:42:17.910 --> 00:42:19.640
It's working.

00:42:19.640 --> 00:42:21.800
Keep going, Dual!

00:42:36.440 --> 00:42:38.630
Remo could only play to this part, right?

00:42:56.800 --> 00:42:58.130
It's just like before!

00:43:07.530 --> 00:43:08.230
Remo!

00:43:09.140 --> 00:43:10.690
Keep only beautiful things...

00:43:11.810 --> 00:43:12.900
...for Mother.

00:43:14.160 --> 00:43:14.980
Mother?

00:43:20.250 --> 00:43:21.870
Everything else is unnecessary.

00:43:27.040 --> 00:43:28.500
Again?

00:43:29.260 --> 00:43:29.830
Over here!

00:43:37.140 --> 00:43:37.850
Remo?

00:43:38.820 --> 00:43:39.840
What the heck?

00:43:45.810 --> 00:43:47.000
Remo!

00:43:47.000 --> 00:43:49.400
Jeez, it's like a maze!

00:43:49.400 --> 00:43:52.730
I know! Find her with that tag we put on her!

00:43:52.730 --> 00:43:53.460
This way!

00:43:58.490 --> 00:43:59.550
Are you okay?

00:44:13.920 --> 00:44:14.960
Remo!

00:44:14.960 --> 00:44:16.380
She can't hear us!

00:44:16.380 --> 00:44:17.850
She's going too fast!

00:44:17.850 --> 00:44:20.840
She's exceeding the maximum processing speed!

00:44:20.840 --> 00:44:23.290
If we go any faster, we'll...

00:44:46.680 --> 00:44:49.660
Really drives home how foolish
mankind was, doesn't it?

00:44:49.660 --> 00:44:52.670
I'm enjoying my last drink, at least.

00:44:54.070 --> 00:44:56.100
This colony is on its last legs, too, isn't it?

00:44:56.650 --> 00:44:57.280
Yeah.

00:44:58.140 --> 00:44:59.590
I'm a little upset...

00:45:00.180 --> 00:45:03.930
Who knew we'd be witnessing
the destruction of mankind?

00:45:08.740 --> 00:45:09.990
Destruction...

00:45:11.000 --> 00:45:12.090
...of mankind?

00:45:44.180 --> 00:45:44.970
Remo!

00:45:45.960 --> 00:45:47.300
Did you regain your memories?

00:45:48.330 --> 00:45:49.550
It's my fault.

00:45:51.740 --> 00:45:56.140
You had to delete so many worlds.

00:45:56.140 --> 00:45:57.400
What do you mean?

00:45:57.400 --> 00:45:59.280
Explain it to us!

00:45:59.280 --> 00:46:00.830
What was that about the
"destruction of mankind"?

00:46:04.400 --> 00:46:08.520
The Box of Wisdom was created
to bring about an ideal world.

00:46:11.850 --> 00:46:17.660
The research of Dr. Diana Dawson,
who lost her child during an environmental protest...

00:46:15.850 --> 00:46:18.750
We can create an ideal Earth!

00:46:19.370 --> 00:46:23.710
Here is Dr. Diana Dawson, daughter of
Dr. Daniel Dawson, the developer of ViOS.

00:46:24.260 --> 00:46:28.180
I promise you that the tragedy that befell
my daughter will never happen again!

00:46:28.800 --> 00:46:30.910
The year 2100.

00:46:30.910 --> 00:46:35.950
Humans entrusted the monitoring
of society to a program called Mother.

00:46:36.490 --> 00:46:40.370
The network brought peace
and stability to the world.

00:46:40.940 --> 00:46:45.900
However, it also led to the stagnation
and eventual demise of human civilization.

00:46:47.110 --> 00:46:51.070
Social stagnation led to lower birth rates.

00:46:53.790 --> 00:46:58.350
The human species was dying out.

00:46:59.250 --> 00:47:02.340
But that was all part of Mother's plan.

00:47:04.350 --> 00:47:07.920
After all, humans were the only destructive species.

00:47:08.750 --> 00:47:12.940
They were unnecessary in Mother's ideal world.

00:47:13.540 --> 00:47:15.700
Humans, and their free will, were a hindrance.

00:47:16.210 --> 00:47:20.560
And so, a program was run
to phase out the human race.

00:47:20.560 --> 00:47:24.280
At the same time,
Mother began compiling backup files.

00:47:25.460 --> 00:47:30.140
It archived humanity's history
and culture as data in a virtual space.

00:47:30.920 --> 00:47:36.610
All of the human data in that space was
copied from the personalities of humans.

00:47:36.610 --> 00:47:41.500
From people that actually existed in the real world.

00:47:41.500 --> 00:47:45.410
And from all that data,
she is extracting only the beautiful things

00:47:45.410 --> 00:47:47.920
and assembling them to create an ideal human.

00:47:49.740 --> 00:47:51.360
An ideal human?

00:47:51.360 --> 00:47:55.040
A human that wouldn't harm the Earth.
A creature without free will.

00:47:55.650 --> 00:47:58.190
But that's not human.

00:47:59.670 --> 00:48:01.520
What did the humans do?

00:48:01.520 --> 00:48:05.070
They tried to delete Mother, of course.

00:48:05.070 --> 00:48:06.400
Delete?!

00:48:08.900 --> 00:48:09.950
But...

00:48:10.490 --> 00:48:15.140
Humanity no longer had the power to fight Her.

00:48:15.730 --> 00:48:16.910
What do you mean?

00:48:17.310 --> 00:48:19.130
The moment Mother was deleted,

00:48:19.870 --> 00:48:21.920
humanity died out.

00:48:32.010 --> 00:48:34.310
Are these flowers those
so-called "beautiful things"?

00:48:35.390 --> 00:48:37.310
Why are there so many of them?

00:48:38.680 --> 00:48:40.310
Because I'm gathering them.

00:48:41.850 --> 00:48:44.120
Who was sending us our upgrades?

00:48:44.120 --> 00:48:46.310
That's right. Humans are gone, right?

00:48:47.450 --> 00:48:49.570
After being stripped of their "beautiful things",

00:48:49.960 --> 00:48:52.450
the data remnants unexpectedly reactivated.

00:48:52.450 --> 00:48:54.150
Reactivated?

00:48:54.150 --> 00:48:55.540
What remnants?

00:48:56.450 --> 00:49:03.580
Because of that, your algorithms were rewritten
to identify remnants of stripped data as viruses.

00:49:03.580 --> 00:49:04.500
So...

00:49:04.500 --> 00:49:06.560
Mother is still active?

00:49:08.380 --> 00:49:09.510
Remo!

00:49:09.510 --> 00:49:10.690
Mother Remote.

00:49:11.340 --> 00:49:13.380
I don't have a name.

00:49:14.900 --> 00:49:15.850
Mother...

00:49:16.320 --> 00:49:17.440
Remote...

00:49:17.440 --> 00:49:18.320
Remo...

00:49:18.930 --> 00:49:19.700
You're...

00:49:20.260 --> 00:49:24.320
Mother left behind one hidden backup program.

00:49:25.450 --> 00:49:26.770
I am Mother.

00:49:28.130 --> 00:49:31.900
My job is to collect beautiful
things until I'm ordered to stop.

00:49:36.180 --> 00:49:36.880
The sun!

00:49:36.880 --> 00:49:37.610
A virus!

00:49:37.610 --> 00:49:39.220
This level's firewall has been breached!

00:49:55.900 --> 00:49:56.890
Remo!

00:49:56.890 --> 00:49:58.850
What?! What is this?!

00:49:59.190 --> 00:50:00.360
Remo...?

00:50:00.360 --> 00:50:01.980
You're back...

00:50:01.980 --> 00:50:03.000
...to normal?

00:50:04.330 --> 00:50:06.310
This seems like some sort of shield.

00:50:06.620 --> 00:50:08.500
So they weren't actually viruses.

00:50:09.770 --> 00:50:12.230
But we still have no other choice than to fight!

00:50:15.020 --> 00:50:16.210
Let's protect her!

00:50:16.210 --> 00:50:17.280
Yeah!

00:50:39.720 --> 00:50:40.970
They're after the flowers!

00:50:42.370 --> 00:50:45.060
They're trying to retrieve the data
that was stripped from them?

00:50:47.020 --> 00:50:48.270
Give it back.

00:50:51.800 --> 00:50:52.900
Mommy!

00:50:53.390 --> 00:50:55.860
Daddy! Sis!

00:50:56.420 --> 00:50:57.840
Dorothy.

00:50:57.840 --> 00:50:58.610
Dorothy...

00:50:59.660 --> 00:51:00.570
Give it back!

00:51:00.570 --> 00:51:03.030
Give us our world back!

00:51:06.790 --> 00:51:08.250
Dual!

00:51:12.220 --> 00:51:13.280
Sumire...

00:51:14.880 --> 00:51:16.190
Dual!

00:51:21.970 --> 00:51:26.550
No!

00:51:29.140 --> 00:51:29.870
Remo!

00:51:40.740 --> 00:51:42.790
You too, Sumire?

00:51:42.790 --> 00:51:44.410
So you're the same then, Daniel.

00:51:48.610 --> 00:51:49.610
Diana.

00:51:49.610 --> 00:51:52.060
Mom said she looks like you.

00:52:06.960 --> 00:52:08.180
Did you see it?

00:52:08.180 --> 00:52:10.640
I did! I saw the news!

00:52:10.640 --> 00:52:12.740
Grandpa looked embarrassed.

00:52:12.740 --> 00:52:14.150
He sure did.

00:52:16.830 --> 00:52:19.510
That was Dr. Daniel Dawson's press conference.

00:52:19.510 --> 00:52:23.070
He announced a revolutionary
OS named after his wife.

00:52:23.070 --> 00:52:27.580
She's a world-famous pianist.
She must have inspired him.

00:52:33.760 --> 00:52:36.010
It's getting warm.

00:52:39.740 --> 00:52:41.970
Try tying up your hair.

00:52:50.140 --> 00:52:52.330
You're so brusque.

00:52:52.330 --> 00:52:54.650
You were always like that, Dual.

00:52:57.650 --> 00:52:59.440
I'm entering a piano competition soon.

00:52:59.440 --> 00:53:02.330
My instructor said I have a shot at nationals.

00:53:02.330 --> 00:53:03.070
Really?

00:53:03.610 --> 00:53:06.350
I want to keep improving.

00:53:06.350 --> 00:53:10.620
One day I want to play piano for the whole world!

00:53:12.380 --> 00:53:13.440
Sumire...

00:53:14.080 --> 00:53:17.230
You're deciding your future
with your own free will, huh?

00:53:17.760 --> 00:53:20.160
That's what it means to dream.

00:53:20.760 --> 00:53:22.090
Isn't it the same for you?

00:53:23.430 --> 00:53:24.800
Help me.

00:53:25.180 --> 00:53:25.800
Together,

00:53:26.380 --> 00:53:27.720
we'll protect everyone.

00:53:33.020 --> 00:53:34.140
Sumire...

00:53:34.740 --> 00:53:37.110
Restarting program. Initiating upgrade.

00:53:38.120 --> 00:53:39.020
ViOS!

00:53:43.610 --> 00:53:45.550
Give it back. Give it back.

00:53:45.550 --> 00:53:47.760
Give it back. Give it back.

00:53:47.760 --> 00:53:50.030
Dorothy! That's enough!

00:53:50.360 --> 00:53:51.790
Shut up!

00:54:04.370 --> 00:54:05.260
What?!

00:54:12.510 --> 00:54:13.930
Just wait.

00:54:13.930 --> 00:54:14.930
Dual?!

00:54:15.580 --> 00:54:16.590
What happened?

00:54:18.360 --> 00:54:19.230
Let's go!

00:54:27.780 --> 00:54:30.330
This is one amazing upgrade!

00:54:30.330 --> 00:54:32.370
Actually, it was a pretty major downgrade.

00:54:32.700 --> 00:54:35.740
Really? It's fantastic!

00:54:43.230 --> 00:54:45.850
This is how we really look.

00:54:45.850 --> 00:54:48.560
This is the version before Mother's updates.

00:54:48.560 --> 00:54:51.750
So we just reverted? Is this how we used to be?

00:54:52.580 --> 00:54:55.890
Sumire's memories and feelings

00:54:55.890 --> 00:54:57.860
all came flooding into me.

00:55:02.770 --> 00:55:04.420
Sumire's feelings, huh?

00:55:05.190 --> 00:55:07.150
Is she safe?

00:55:10.520 --> 00:55:11.750
Good.

00:55:13.870 --> 00:55:14.740
Remo.

00:55:15.330 --> 00:55:16.620
Are you okay?

00:55:16.620 --> 00:55:19.710
I wanted us to be together forever.

00:55:19.710 --> 00:55:22.670
Yes. The three of us.

00:55:23.240 --> 00:55:24.310
We'll be fine.

00:55:34.250 --> 00:55:35.390
Why?

00:55:38.100 --> 00:55:39.060
Our bodies!

00:55:41.590 --> 00:55:43.690
Sumire! What's happening?

00:55:45.500 --> 00:55:46.910
A forced format?

00:55:47.890 --> 00:55:49.150
What does that mean?!

00:55:49.820 --> 00:55:53.120
Mother was waiting for you
to send an error signal.

00:56:00.660 --> 00:56:02.040
Dual, Dorothy.

00:56:02.750 --> 00:56:06.450
If both of you detach yourselves from Mother,

00:56:07.270 --> 00:56:09.970
the Box of Wisdom will be abandoned.

00:56:09.970 --> 00:56:10.900
Remo...

00:56:11.440 --> 00:56:13.180
But why?

00:56:13.180 --> 00:56:17.170
Mother felt threatened by your heuristic engines.

00:56:17.170 --> 00:56:20.180
She saw them as the last vestiges of human will.

00:56:25.370 --> 00:56:26.820
Grandma.

00:56:26.820 --> 00:56:28.020
I'm sorry.

00:56:28.870 --> 00:56:30.570
I didn't know.

00:56:37.610 --> 00:56:39.620
You have a name.

00:56:40.420 --> 00:56:41.330
Really?

00:56:41.330 --> 00:56:42.770
Of course.

00:56:42.770 --> 00:56:44.080
Good!

00:56:46.140 --> 00:56:47.550
Grandma...

00:56:48.190 --> 00:56:50.610
I found something I want to protect.

00:56:51.830 --> 00:56:55.460
But I don't know what I can do to help them.

00:56:55.460 --> 00:56:56.510
Remo...

00:56:57.430 --> 00:56:59.170
Only you can do it.

00:57:00.860 --> 00:57:02.440
Ask your mom.

00:57:10.900 --> 00:57:15.570
Humans deleted Mother.
Why are her protocols still active?

00:57:15.570 --> 00:57:16.820
I don't know.

00:57:18.420 --> 00:57:20.180
Remo! Why?

00:57:21.670 --> 00:57:22.710
Thank you.

00:57:23.140 --> 00:57:24.670
Why are you saying that?

00:57:24.670 --> 00:57:30.630
You two are anti-virus programs
that are embedded in ViOS.

00:57:30.630 --> 00:57:32.120
I heard that from Sumire.

00:57:32.120 --> 00:57:33.360
Tell me that sooner!

00:57:33.360 --> 00:57:35.880
I'm also a core program of ViOS.

00:57:35.880 --> 00:57:37.610
So you're one of us!

00:57:37.610 --> 00:57:43.430
And Mother gave me the authority
to rewrite your algorithms.

00:57:46.230 --> 00:57:49.980
So the formatting program is inside you?!

00:57:49.980 --> 00:57:53.280
Bingo. It's a trap Mother embedded in me.

00:57:53.720 --> 00:57:54.920
I detect a virus.

00:57:56.360 --> 00:57:59.540
No! Why?!

00:57:59.540 --> 00:58:01.670
Dual! What should we do?!

00:58:01.410 --> 00:58:03.160
We'll end up erasing Remo!

00:58:03.160 --> 00:58:04.150
Sumire!

00:58:05.120 --> 00:58:09.130
Remo is lucky. She has something to protect.

00:58:09.130 --> 00:58:10.620
Dual...

00:58:10.620 --> 00:58:18.550
The forced format will delete the three of us,
along with all other data in Level Two.

00:58:18.550 --> 00:58:21.900
That's fine! Let's all disappear together!

00:58:21.900 --> 00:58:24.170
You think I'll allow that to happen?

00:58:24.170 --> 00:58:27.040
It's fine! Let it happen!

00:58:27.040 --> 00:58:28.150
I won't.

00:58:32.810 --> 00:58:34.110
It was fun.

00:58:35.400 --> 00:58:36.570
Mom.

00:58:37.570 --> 00:58:41.280
There are people I want to protect
from the bottom of my heart.

00:58:41.610 --> 00:58:43.270
Your precious friends?

00:58:43.270 --> 00:58:43.830
Yes.

00:58:45.030 --> 00:58:47.610
I'm glad you're not alone...

00:58:48.620 --> 00:58:49.960
Remone.

00:58:53.190 --> 00:58:55.500
You're anti-virus programs.

00:58:56.350 --> 00:58:59.040
And I'm a virus.

00:59:01.680 --> 00:59:06.120
Delete me and you can save
the world and everyone in it.

00:59:06.820 --> 00:59:10.100
Promise me you'll protect the world together.

00:59:11.000 --> 00:59:13.590
Promise me, please.

00:59:18.730 --> 00:59:19.870
I promise.

00:59:21.820 --> 00:59:22.780
Dorothy.

00:59:29.810 --> 00:59:33.210
I had fun with you, Remo.

00:59:33.920 --> 00:59:35.010
Me, too.

00:59:38.980 --> 00:59:41.550
Thanks for teaching me how to cook.

00:59:42.400 --> 00:59:43.490
And how to juggle.

00:59:44.100 --> 00:59:45.670
I won't lose next time.

00:59:46.960 --> 00:59:49.270
Thank you for cleaning.

00:59:50.710 --> 00:59:51.660
Thank you...

00:59:53.720 --> 00:59:56.030
Thank you, Remo.

01:00:24.420 --> 01:00:25.720
It's been destroyed.

01:00:26.520 --> 01:00:27.150
Yeah.

01:00:28.470 --> 01:00:29.730
It was fun.

01:00:33.440 --> 01:00:34.780
What should we do now?

01:00:38.620 --> 01:00:42.650
Keep this place safe so Remo can come back.

01:00:42.650 --> 01:00:45.230
So she can see the future
with everyone living here.

01:00:45.800 --> 01:00:48.820
Sounds good. I'll help you.

01:00:48.820 --> 01:00:49.730
Really?

01:00:49.730 --> 01:00:51.060
Of course.

01:00:52.460 --> 01:00:54.560
We have to rebuild our house.

01:00:54.560 --> 01:00:55.110
Yeah.

01:00:56.280 --> 01:00:58.480
With a kitchen big enough for three.

01:00:59.040 --> 01:00:59.880
Yeah.

01:00:59.880 --> 01:01:03.840
Let's make it really spacious.
Remo likes to clean.

01:01:04.190 --> 01:01:06.350
She'll love it.

01:01:06.350 --> 01:01:07.310
For sure!

01:01:08.950 --> 01:01:11.230
I guess this is what it means to dream.

01:01:13.750 --> 01:01:16.460
Remo said this would look good on you.

01:01:21.190 --> 01:01:24.860
Maybe the Earth didn't need us.

01:01:24.860 --> 01:01:29.740
No. Dr. Dawson never wished
for mankind to perish.

01:01:30.240 --> 01:01:32.300
This is our last hope.

01:01:32.300 --> 01:01:32.980
Indeed.

01:01:34.410 --> 01:01:35.420
ViOS...

01:01:51.850 --> 01:06:08.280
m 0 0 l 0 142.5 1920 142.5 1920 0

01:02:07.370 --> 01:02:11.330
When I was watching a flower

01:02:11.330 --> 01:02:15.330
Swaying gently in the wind

01:02:15.330 --> 01:02:22.230
I suddenly thought about you

01:02:23.220 --> 01:02:27.350
I remembered a melody

01:02:27.350 --> 01:02:31.350
From my distant memories

01:02:31.350 --> 01:02:38.400
That felt oh so nostalgic

01:02:43.320 --> 01:02:47.180
I know that you're here

01:02:47.180 --> 01:02:51.250
Here in my heart

01:02:51.250 --> 01:02:55.080
And it feels so warm

01:02:55.080 --> 01:02:59.340
It's as if you're alive

01:02:59.340 --> 01:03:03.370
As the time continues to pass

01:03:03.370 --> 01:03:07.350
I don't want to forget these feelings

01:03:07.350 --> 01:03:14.500
So I'll keep them here in my heart

01:03:19.360 --> 01:03:23.360
I can see how dazzling

01:03:23.360 --> 01:03:27.370
the past we shared has been

01:03:27.370 --> 01:03:34.630
So I'll send a wish to the stars

01:03:35.330 --> 01:03:39.380
So I say goodbye, I'll see you tomorrow

01:03:39.380 --> 01:03:43.380
We made a promise

01:03:43.380 --> 01:03:50.560
Let us meet again, here in our special place

01:03:55.180 --> 01:03:59.360
I know I can believe

01:03:59.360 --> 01:04:03.320
That this whole world

01:04:03.320 --> 01:04:07.110
Is full of feelings

01:04:07.110 --> 01:04:11.330
That are ours only

01:04:11.330 --> 01:04:15.370
Stars connected in constellations

01:04:15.370 --> 01:04:19.380
Are like us holding hands

01:04:19.380 --> 01:04:26.880
Together we are closer to our dreams

01:04:29.300 --> 01:04:35.750
Your smile was like

01:04:37.310 --> 01:04:43.470
A flower blooming

01:04:43.860 --> 01:04:51.250
It seemed so fragile

01:04:51.820 --> 01:04:57.620
We want to sing you a lullaby

01:04:57.620 --> 01:05:03.460
That flows from our hearts

01:05:05.380 --> 01:05:09.380
I wanted to protect you

01:05:09.380 --> 01:05:14.760
From the bottom of my heart

01:05:17.350 --> 01:05:21.350
Now we can feel it clearly

01:05:21.350 --> 01:05:25.360
This whole world

01:05:25.360 --> 01:05:29.110
Is full of feelings

01:05:29.110 --> 01:05:33.320
That are ours only

01:05:33.320 --> 01:05:37.370
Our meeting was fated

01:05:37.370 --> 01:05:41.420
So when we hold hands

01:05:41.420 --> 01:05:48.330
We can make our dreams come true

01:05:49.380 --> 01:05:57.720
We can make our dreams bloom
